WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.720
A busy café.

2
00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:05.120
Two friends spot a free
table, and one of them says:

3
00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:06.580
shall we sit down?

4
00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.560
Now a head's office.

5
00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:10.370
A nameplate on the door.

6
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:14.510
The head looks up at a student
and says exactly the same words.

7
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.180
Same words.

8
00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.150
But do they mean the same thing?

9
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.300
How does the head's version
differ from the friend's?

10
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:24.710
In this mission, you'll
ask where power comes from:

11
00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.680
a job title, or a way with words?

12
00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:31.800
You'll learn how polite forms
protect what linguists call face:

13
00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:34.250
the self-image we all want to keep.

14
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.050
And you'll sit in on a
meeting in the head's office,

15
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.560
line by line.

16
00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:42.700
Your mission: explain how the head's
words differ from the friend's.
